diff --git a/docs/labwc-actions.5.scd b/docs/labwc-actions.5.scd
index 53e40a20..9e343841 100644
--- a/docs/labwc-actions.5.scd
+++ b/docs/labwc-actions.5.scd
@@ -129,6 +129,50 @@ Actions are used in menus and keyboard/mouse bindings.
 	Resize and move the active window back to its untiled or unmaximized
 	position if it had been maximized or tiled to a direction or region.
 
+*<action name="DirectionalCycleWindows" direction="north" />*
+	Select windows spatially while the binding's modifiers are held. Supported
+	directions are *north*, *south*, *east*, and *west*. Each key press moves
+	from the selected window (initially the focused window). Holding the key
+	does not repeat. If there is no focused window, nothing happens.
+
+	Windows are located by their content center in desktop coordinates.
+	North/south selects the nearest strictly smaller/larger Y coordinate;
+	east/west uses X. Ties prefer the smallest distance along the other axis,
+	then the most recently focused window. Equal coordinates on the requested
+	axis are excluded. There is no wrapping: no candidate leaves the selection
+	unchanged. Window overlap and visibility do not affect the ordering.
+
+	Candidates include minimized windows and windows on the current workspace
+	(including omnipresent windows), across all outputs. Panels and desktop
+	windows are excluded. A thick outline shows the selection, using the
+	window-switcher preview border colors and a minimum border width of 2.
+	Windows are not raised or restored during selection; a minimized window's
+	outline marks its retained position. No switcher dialog is displayed.
+
+	Releasing all modifiers commits the selection. Escape cancels without
+	running final actions. Closing the selected window cancels selection too.
+	NextWindow/PreviousWindow are ignored during directional selection.
+
+	*finalactions*: Nested actions to run on the selected window, in order.
+	If omitted, defaults to *Focus*, *Raise*, *Unshade*. An explicit list
+	replaces the defaults, and an empty list runs nothing. The binding which
+	starts selection supplies the final actions for the entire selection.
+
+	Example:
+
+```
+<keybind key="W-Up">
+  <action name="DirectionalCycleWindows">
+    <direction>north</direction>
+    <finalactions>
+      <action name="Focus" />
+      <action name="Raise" />
+      <action name="Unshade" />
+    </finalactions>
+  </action>
+</keybind>
+```
+
 *<action name="NextWindow" workspace="current" output="all" identifier="all" />*++
 *<action name="PreviousWindow" workspace="current" output="all" identifier="all" />*++
 *<action name="NextWindowImmediate" workspace="current" output="all" identifier="all" />*++
